    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Jacinta has $\\frac{2}{3}$ of a litre of water in a jug and then pours in $\\frac{1}{4}$ of a litre. How much water is in the jug now?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{11}{12}$ of a litre of water.",
      "worked": "The LCM of 3 and 4 is 12.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}&=\\frac{8}{12}+\\frac{3}{12}\\\\\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}&=\\frac{11}{12}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThere is $\\frac{11}{12}$ of a litre of water in the jug.",
